<section class="border-b border-border/40">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-24">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-muted mb-6">
      01 · The gap
    </p>
    <h2 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-ink tracking-tight mb-8">
      The agent does not remember. It re&#8209;reads.
    </h2>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-10 text-ink-dim leading-relaxed">
      <div>
        <p class="text-base">
          Every Claude Code session boots from scratch. The model is the
          same. The <em class="text-ink">agent</em> that knows its person's
          shorthand, corrections and open work is gone.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-base">
          Essence does not give the agent a memory. It gives the agent
          files to read. A new session reads them and starts from what is
          written.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="text-base">
          That has two results. First, the files have to be small enough to
          read whole every time. Second, the writing has to be careful.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-base">
          What the agent writes today is
          <span class="text-ember">who shows up tomorrow</span>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
